course: dictionary
lesson: 14403
title: Outstretched arms
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The little girl ran across the park with her arms outstretched.» Outstretched is made of out and stretched. Her arms are stretched out as far as they can go, so outstretched means stretched out as far as possible.
explain: Look at the words around it. Her arms are the part of her body that is stretched. Running towards someone with arms wide open is a clue that she wants a hug.
explain: The same word can show different things. A hand can be outstretched to say hello, to ask for help, or to catch someone who is falling. The sentence around it tells you which one.
fact: Outstretched means stretched out as far as possible.
fact: It is usually used for arms, hands, wings or legs.
fact: «With arms outstretched» is a common phrase in stories, and it often shows a welcome or a hug.
fact: «Outstretched» can also mean reaching out to save someone, as in «an outstretched hand».
fact: A good check is to swap in «stretched out» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The eagle glided over the hills, its wings outstretched.» What does outstretched mean here? | Flying backwards | Covered in mud | Folded tightly against its body | *Stretched out as far as possible
exercise: «Mum ran down the path with her arms outstretched, and I ran straight into her hug.» What do the outstretched arms show? | Anger at the rain | Tiredness after a long walk | *A welcome | A warning to stop
exercise: «The dancers stood in a line with their legs outstretched.» Find and copy one word that is a body part. | stood | dancers | *legs | outstretched
test: «He grabbed my wrist with an outstretched hand just before I slipped into the river.» What is the outstretched hand doing? | Waving goodbye | Keeping very still | *Reaching out to save me | Holding a pencil
test: «In PE, we lay on the mat with our arms and legs outstretched like a star.» Which body position is this? | Sitting cross-legged | Curled up in a tight ball | *A star shape with limbs spread wide | Standing on one leg
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The bird flew off with its wings outstretched»? | Tucked in close to its body | Shaking with cold | Pointing at the sun | *Spread out wide as far as they can go
